  {
   "id": "5tcECsZOFwAJ",
   "from": "Terrence Jorgensen",
   "author": "3fe90052fbf2f899",
   "date": "2018-09-24T09:38:11Z",
   "subject": "Re: LAVAAN - Help with longitudinal measurements",
   "parts": [
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div>I would like NOT to use common itens in the measurements.Is this possible?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>No, you need some linking items in order to link the scales of the latent traits across time.  Without overlapping items, you have no basis for linking scales.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div>My understanding is that<br></div><div><br></div><div>With Model 1, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will <b>be different</b>. Is this correct?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Yes.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div>With Model 2, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will <b>be the same</b>. Is this correct?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>No, but they can be put on the same scale by applying equality constraints to the loadings over time. </div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div><br></div><div>With Model 3, the scale of the items in moments 1 and 2 will <b>be the same</b>. The assumption here is that the items will be equated with the linking test. Is this correct? </div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>Only if you can constrain the loadings of the common items across time.</div></div>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div><br></div><blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0;margin-left:0.8ex;border-left:1px #ccc solid;padding-left:1ex\"><div dir=\"ltr\"><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div>If yes, how can  I pass these info to LAVAAN?</div></div></div></blockquote><div><br></div></div>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><div>In lavaan&#39;s model syntax, you can apply the same label to multiple parameters.  Parameters with the same label will have the same estimated value.  For example, if items &quot;x&quot; measure Time 1 and items &quot;y&quot; measure Time 2, and items 1-3 are in common across time:</div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"background-color:rgb(250,250,250);border-color:rgb(187,187,187);border-style:solid;border-width:1px\"><code><div><span style=\"color:#000\">model </span><span style=\"color:#660\">&lt;-</span><span style=\"color:#000\"> </span><span style=\"color:#080\">&#39; <br>    T1 =~ L1*x1 + L2*x2 + L3*x3 + x4 + x5<br>    T2 =~ L1*y1 + L2*y2 + L3*y3 + y6 + y7<br>&#39;</span></div></code></div><div><br></div></div><div><br></div><div><div style=\"font-size:small\"><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Terrence D. Jorgensen</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Postdoctoral Researcher, Methods and Statistics</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\">Research Institute for Child Development and Education, the University of Amsterdam</div><div style=\"font-size:13px\"><a href=\"http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen\" style=\"color:rgb(17,85,204)\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792424848449000&amp;usg=AOvVaw3YDxl56lWtu53SWfhsHP_D\">http://www.uva.nl/profile/t.d.jorgensen</a></div><div><br></div></div></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
